Creator: Minh
1. What this website is: A calendar to-do website is a productivity platform that merges task management (your to-do list) with scheduling (your calendar) into one unified interface. Instead of managing tasks and meetings in separate apps, these websites let you drag-and-drop tasks directly into specific time slots on your calendar.
2. How it uses the data files in data: Default data will be calendar, but you will generate different users with different calendar events. The goal is something like Google Calendar
3. What real world websites it should be modeled after: Google Calendar, Outlook Calendar, ...
4. Whether the domain has temporal/dynamic data (and how it should simulate): this domain is relatively dynamic in nature
5. Any domain-specific behavior or constraints: users have to be able create and modify events at least. You will have to emulate most of Google Calendar functionalities.